Guns are also called `` firearms '' . In military terms , the word `` firearm '' is usually used for the type of weapons that soldiers carry -LRB- pistols and rifles -RRB- , while the word `` gun '' is used for larger guns that fire at higher speed . The weapons on warships and tanks are called `` guns '' or `` turrets '' -LRB- if placed on a rotating base -RRB- , not `` firearms '' .
When the king or queen of a hereditary monarchy dies or quits the throne -LRB- abdicates -RRB- , the crown is generally passed to one of his or her children , often to the oldest . When that child dies , the crown will be then passed to his or her child , or , if he or she has no child , to a sister , brother , niece , nephew , cousin , or some other relative .
